// Merging use statements leaves a two-statement block with one, which
// does not parse: the formatter refuses with "formatter bug" on text that
// parses (the use in the value slot is refused later, by the compile).
//
// Run: graphix fmt --stdout design/review-2026-10-19/repro/t-format-resolver-merge-empties-block.gx
// Expected: the file back unchanged, or the uses merged only where a
//           block keeps two statements
// Observed: formatter bug: the formatted text does not parse: ...
//           a block must contain at least 2 expressions
//               let f = |x| { use array::{len, map} };
let f = |x| { use array::len; use array::map };
1
